# jemdoc: menu{MENU}{htmlchanges.html}
= jemdocx -- HTML configuration

jemdocx has a built-in configuration containing the HTML fragments used to
generate a page. A configuration file can override any named block without
copying the rest of the defaults.

Print the complete default configuration with:

~~~
{}{sh}
python3 jemdoc --show-config
~~~

== Example: customize the footer
The default +\[lastupdated\]+ block controls the generated footer text. Create a
file named +site.conf+ containing:

~~~
{site.conf}{}
[lastupdated]
Updated | with jemdocx.
~~~

Use the configuration while generating a page:

~~~
{}{sh}
python3 jemdoc -c site.conf index.jemdoc
~~~

The vertical bar is replaced with the page's generated timestamp. Other blocks
can change stylesheets, document structure, menu markup, scripts, or footer
behavior. Configuration files are UTF-8 text and may define only the blocks
that differ from the defaults.

For analytics, prefer the built-in +analytics{TAG_ID}+ modeline described on
the [modelines.html modelines page]. It emits the current HTTPS Google tag
snippet; site owners remain responsible for consent and privacy requirements.
